write,32768,6,32768
write,65536,14,65536
BASELINE PASS
$

The benchmark values use the kernel's coarse global `uptime()` tick counter and include only the user `write()` call. The concurrent-write check verifies the resulting file has the expected length and only bytes written by either child; it is a functional smoke test, not a formal atomicity guarantee.

