Repeat trial 2
--------------
The baseline kernel was rebuilt from the same historical revision in a detached
worktree. QEMU 10.2.4 was run with the same x86 machine, 512 MB RAM, filesystem
size, and CPU counts. The measurement program was copied from the repository's
`baseline.c`; `_baseline` was passed through `UPROGS` without changing the
baseline kernel source. Each run completed with `BASELINE PASS`.

CPUS=1, trial=2
benchmark,size_bytes,elapsed_ticks,bytes_written
write,1024,5,1024
write,2048,4,2048
write,4096,23,4096
write,8192,11,8192
write,16384,31,16384
write,32768,75,32768
write,65536,146,65536

CPUS=3, trial=2
benchmark,size_bytes,elapsed_ticks,bytes_written
write,1024,12,1024
write,2048,21,2048
write,4096,49,4096
write,8192,65,8192
write,16384,58,16384
write,32768,162,32768
write,65536,336,65536

The large spread from trial 1 confirms that tick resolution and emulator
scheduling dominate these measurements. Treat them as functional baseline
evidence only; they do not support a reliable performance comparison.
